# Canonical LF in the repo AND in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true checks files out as CRLF on Windows while
# Prettier's endOfLine:"lf" expects LF — which failed ~20 files on line endings
# alone and printed "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on every commit. Pinning eol
# here also means format:check cannot disagree between CI and a dev box.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets, declared explicitly rather than left to the text=auto
# heuristic. That matters most for the Illustrator source under Reference
# Materials: it is PDF-based, so it opens with ASCII ("%PDF-1.6\r%...") and git's
# own diff machinery already reports it as 2287 lines of text. Only the
# NUL-byte check in the conversion path is currently keeping eol=lf from
# stripping its carriage returns and corrupting it — too thin a thread to hang a
# binary asset on.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.ai   binary

# SVG, CSV and the dev-panel .txt profiles are genuinely text and should be
# normalised like everything else — they are deliberately not listed above.
